Task: Scaffold the NeuroPulse SDET Training Course Slide Deck

You are working in the existing NeuroPulse SDET training repository.

The NeuroPulse application has already been built and tested successfully.

Your next task is to scaffold the instructor slide deck for the first two phases of the SDET programme.

Do not build PowerPoint files.

Instead, create a well-structured Markdown slide deck that can later be used by an instructor to build PowerPoint slides.

The training is deliberately practical.

The instructor does not want to lecture continuously.

Each training day is 4½ hours long, and the desired teaching rhythm is:

15–20 minutes instructor-led concepts
        ↓
practical activity / investigation / discussion
        ↓
brief review / debrief
        ↓
next concept

Avoid sections requiring more than about 20 minutes of uninterrupted explanation.

The deck should therefore feel more like a sequence of:

Explain → Explore → Apply → Reflect

than:

Lecture → Lecture → Lecture → Exercise at end

